model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The pool controller says what happened to it. Each construction writes one POOL_CONTROLLER_INSTANCE line with an isolate identifier named on first use, the isolate's age, a construction count and whether the container was already running, so a new isolate shows a platform replacement and a later construction in the same isolate shows a rebuilt object. A model stream whose upstream read fails in the controller writes one POOL_STREAM_BROKEN line, at most three a second, with the place it broke and the error's closed name, code and message class and the platform's retryable, overloaded, remote and reset flags, never its text. The native stream wrapper parses at most 1,048,576 characters of one unfinished event; past that it stops parsing and passes the rest through unchanged, so one endless event cannot grow memory or time with its square."
    }
  }
}
